---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import study from "../data/banking77-balanced.json";

const percent = (value: number) => `${(value * 100).toFixed(2)}%`;
const money = (value: number) => `$${value.toFixed(6)}`;
const sourceUrl = `https://github.com/PolyAI-LDN/task-specific-datasets/tree/${study.source_revision}/banking_data`;
---

<Base title="Verdict — BANKING77 research results" description="A balanced exploratory comparison of OpenAI Decisions, Jev Direct, Clef, and Clef Flash on 154 BANKING77 messages across 77 intents.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Verdict research · October 8, 2026 · Exploratory experiment</p>
  <h1>Four decision APIs. The same 154 messages.</h1>
  <p class="tagline">How do dedicated decision APIs compare when they receive the same labeled
    tasks and allowed choices? We tested OpenAI Decisions, Jev Direct, Clef, and Clef Flash
    on a balanced sample of BANKING77, using shared definitions and all 77 intent labels.</p>
  <p class="links"><a href="/research/banking77-balanced.md">Read the full research report</a>
    <a href="/playground">Try the local playground</a></p>

  <div class="run-facts" aria-label="Experiment scope">
    <div><strong>{study.n_messages}</strong><span>labeled messages per API</span></div>
    <div><strong>{study.n_intents}</strong><span>intents · two messages each</span></div>
    <div><strong>{study.n_attempts}</strong><span>attempts · no retries</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="callout"><strong>A completed small sample, not the full BANKING77 benchmark.</strong>
    Two messages per intent are too few for stable intent-level conclusions.
    The design followed an earlier experiment; 12 messages were previously attempted.
    All results below are new observations, with earlier outputs kept separate.</p>

  <h2>Observed results</h2>
  <p class="table-note">Each API attempted the same 154 messages. Accuracy counts failures as incorrect.
    A valid wrong label reduces accuracy but is not a response failure. API order is fixed below;
    it is not a ranking.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="BANKING77 results" tabindex="0">
    <table class="board">
      <caption class="sr-only">Results from 154 messages per API, October 8, 2026</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">API</th><th scope="col">Correct / attempted</th>
        <th scope="col">Accuracy</th><th scope="col">Failures</th>
        <th scope="col">Median / p95 latency</th><th scope="col">Cost / 154 attempts</th>
        <th scope="col">Billing basis / coverage</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{study.providers.map(provider => <tr>
        <th scope="row">{provider.name}</th>
        <td class="num">{provider.correct} / {provider.attempted}</td>
        <td class="num">{percent(provider.accuracy)}</td>
        <td class="num">{provider.failures}</td>
        <td class="num">{Math.round(provider.median_valid_wall_ms)} / {Math.round(provider.p95_valid_wall_ms)} ms</td>
        <td class="num">{provider.total_cost_usd === null
          ? <><strong>Unknown total</strong><br />{money(provider.known_cost_subtotal_usd)} known subtotal</>
          : money(provider.total_cost_usd)}</td>
        <td class="billing">{provider.cost_basis.kind}<br />{provider.known_cost_count} / {provider.attempted} attempts priced</td>
      </tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="table-note">Latency is median and p95 client wall time for valid responses from one Windows
    machine in Bangladesh. It includes network and gateway overhead. Three-second scheduling
    intervals and cooldown waits are excluded. The report also includes all-attempt latency.</p>
  <p class="table-note">Costs include failed attempts when usage is known. OpenAI uses a published
    input-token estimate; OpenRouter routes use reported charges. These are not verified invoice
    totals. Flash’s two unpriced failures make its total unknown.</p>

  <h2>What we observed</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Clef returned 146 correct decisions and Clef Flash 145. A one-message difference
      does not establish that one is better.</li>
    <li>OpenAI had the lowest median latency in this run. Jev had the lowest reported charge.</li>
    <li>OpenAI returned one refusal. Flash had a connection reset and a temporary-capacity
      HTTP 429 rejection. Both failed attempts were retained; neither was retried.</li>
  </ul>

  <details>
    <summary>How the sample and measurements were fixed</summary>
    <p>We used the authors’ official test split: 3,080 messages, 40 per intent. A fixed
      random seed ({study.seed}) selected two messages from each intent, then shuffled their
      order before live calls. Shared definitions were developed from training examples and
      stayed unchanged. Each request allowed all 77 labels.</p>
    <p>Calls ran sequentially, with provider order rotated per message. No client retries,
      cache, fallback, or escalation. After two access failures, saved evidence and billing
      holds were audited before continuing only unattempted pairs. All 616 observations
      passed offline source/request/reply verification, with zero unfinished starts.</p>
    <p>Jev, Clef, and Flash used OpenRouter’s Decisions API; native OpenAI used its own
      Decisions endpoint. Cloudflare was pinned with fallbacks disabled. Reported model IDs
      are provider claims, not independent verification of model weights.</p>
    <p><a href={sourceUrl}>BANKING77 source revision</a> · CC-BY-4.0 ·
      Iñigo Casanueva, Tadas Temčinas, Daniela Gerz, Matthew Henderson, and Ivan Vulić,
      <em>Efficient Intent Detection with Dual Sentence Encoders</em> (2020).</p>
    <p class="fingerprint">Sample fingerprint: <code>{study.selection_sha256}</code></p>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Per-intent counts: two messages per API</summary>
    <p class="table-note">Cells show correct / attempted, then failures. Two messages per intent
      give limited evidence; these counts should not guide an intent-specific provider choice.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Per-intent results" tabindex="0">
      <table class="board"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Intent</th>
        {study.providers.map(provider => <th scope="col">{provider.name}</th>)}</tr></thead>
        <tbody>{study.label_order.map(label => <tr><th scope="row">{label}</th>
          {study.providers.map(provider => {
            const counts = provider.by_intent[label];
            return <td class="num">{counts.correct} / {counts.attempted} ({counts.failures} failures)</td>;
          })}</tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </details>

  <p class="next-note">These saved results make no API calls when viewed.
    <a href="/comparison">Earlier 24-ticket comparison</a> ·
    <a href="/historical">Historical leaderboard</a> · <a href="/methodology">Methodology</a>.
    A second domain and repeated runs would help test whether these findings generalize.</p>
</Base>

<style>
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-2); margin-top: 30px; font-size: 13px; }
  h1 { margin-top: 8px; }
  .links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px 24px; }
  .run-facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 12px; margin: 26px 0; }
  .run-facts > div { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px; }
  .run-facts strong { display: block; font-size: 26px; }
  .run-facts span, .table-note, .next-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .table-scroll:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 3px; }
  table.board th { cursor: default; }
  table.board tbody th { text-transform: none; letter-spacing: normal; color: var(--text); }
  table.board .billing { white-space: normal; min-width: 190px; text-align: left; font-size: 12px; }
  details { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin: 20px 0; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }
  details p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  .fingerprint code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .sr-only { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden; clip-path: inset(50%); white-space: nowrap; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .run-facts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
